# OWNER-LOGIN DEPLOYMENT — Compose INTERPOLATION values for docker-compose.image.yml and its overrides
# (docker compose --env-file <this file>). NO SECRET belongs here: only image references, host paths, the API bind
# address/port and resource limits. Copy to e.g. /etc/crewflow/compose.env (root:root 0600). Passing --env-file also stops
# Compose from reading a stray .env next to the compose files.
# Lint it: node packages/rab-docker/scripts/compose-owner-login.cjs --lint-env-file compose /etc/crewflow/compose.env
#
# Image: the approved release's multi-platform INDEX digest (amd64 + arm64), never a tag. ONE image runs the API (which
# migrates on start, O3), the Worker and rab-ops (O1/O2; published under the one tag <full commit>; take the digest from the release
# manifest). The retired CREWFLOW_API_IMAGE_DIGEST / CREWFLOW_WORKER_IMAGE_DIGEST are refused here.
CREWFLOW_IMAGE_DIGEST=sha256:<image-index-digest-64-hex>
# Only to override the release registry (default adhin007/adolphus):
# CREWFLOW_IMAGE_REPOSITORY=<registry/repository>
#
# Migration approval (BC-11, C4): unset = none, the API applies pending migrations on start without a token (like
# Twenty). token = opt-in safety net: an API start that would apply to a non-fresh database needs
# CREWFLOW_MIGRATION_APPROVED=<token> for exactly the pending set (passed to that one start only, never in a file). Set it
# HERE only: the lint refuses it in database.env / runtime.env, where rab-api's committed value would override it.
# CREWFLOW_MIGRATION_APPROVAL_MODE=token
# Redis 7.x and (bundled database only) PostgreSQL 16 alpine, each pinned by digest; record the tag each was resolved from.
CREWFLOW_REDIS_IMAGE=redis@sha256:<redis-7-alpine-index-digest-64-hex>
CREWFLOW_POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres@sha256:<postgres-16-alpine-index-digest-64-hex>
#
# Host paths (absolute). The secret directory (root 0700) holds database.env, runtime.env, redis-users.acl and, for the
# bundled database, pg-tls/{ca.crt,server.crt,server.key}, postgres-superuser-password and crewflow-owner-password.
CREWFLOW_SECRETS_DIR=/etc/crewflow/secrets
# The CA certificate for TLS verify-full: the provider's CA bundle, or ${CREWFLOW_SECRETS_DIR}/pg-tls/ca.crt for the
# bundled database.
CREWFLOW_PG_CA_FILE=/etc/crewflow/pg-ca.crt
#
# The address and host port the edge proxy connects to. Never 0.0.0.0. Pick a free host port when another service already
# uses 3000 on this host (Oracle VM: OWNER-LOGIN-ORACLE-VM-PLAN.md).
CREWFLOW_API_BIND=127.0.0.1
CREWFLOW_API_HOST_PORT=3000
#
# Resource limits (cpus must not exceed the host's vCPU count; Docker refuses to start the container otherwise).
CREWFLOW_API_MEM_LIMIT=1024m
CREWFLOW_API_CPUS=2
CREWFLOW_WORKER_MEM_LIMIT=1536m
CREWFLOW_WORKER_CPUS=2
CREWFLOW_REDIS_MAXMEMORY=384mb
CREWFLOW_POSTGRES_MEM_LIMIT=1024m
CREWFLOW_POSTGRES_CPUS=2
#
# MUST NOT BE SET here: any password, URL, token (CREWFLOW_MIGRATION_APPROVED included) or other secret, and any
# application variable (NODE_ENV, PG_*, REDIS_URL, APP_SECRET, CREWFLOW_DB_MODE, ...). COMPOSE_FILE / COMPOSE_PROFILES /
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME: name the files explicitly with -f instead.
